Shader compile: the compiler's size argument is strlen of the source (as Strikers 2564de4)

Same value as s->size on every path that reaches compile_shader (only
glShaderSource writes s->size, except commit_shader_candidate, which sets
s->prog together with it, and compile_shader returns when s->prog is set),
but taken from the text the compiler parses, as the Strikers port's fix
does, so it cannot depend on that bookkeeping.
---
 source/custom_shaders.c | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/source/custom_shaders.c b/source/custom_shaders.c
index 1419be6..0f1f8cd 100644
--- a/source/custom_shaders.c
+++ b/source/custom_shaders.c
@@ -810,9 +810,13 @@ static inline __attribute__((always_inline)) void compile_shader(shader *s, GLbo
 		return;
 	shader candidate = {0};
 	// The compiler owns its output. Do not publish it or clobber the source length.
-	// (galaxy: the size argument is in/out: vitaShaRK reads the SOURCE length from it (shark_input.size = *size) and writes
-	// the program size back. The Strikers port passed 0 here, so the compiler was handed an empty source.)
-	candidate.size = s->size;
+	// The size argument is in/out: vitaShaRK reads the SOURCE length from it (shark_input.size = *size, see the disassembly of
+	// libvitashark.a) and writes the program size back. The Strikers port first passed 0 here (the compiler got an empty file,
+	// "fatal internal error on line -1", for every fresh compile; fixed there in 2564de4 the same way). s->size would also be
+	// the source length on every path that reaches here (only glShaderSource writes it, except commit_shader_candidate, which
+	// sets s->prog at the same time, and compile_shader returns at once when s->prog is set), but strlen of the text the
+	// compiler parses does not depend on that. The source is NUL-terminated by glShaderSource.
+	candidate.size = (uint32_t)strlen((const char *)s->source);
 	const SceGxmProgram *output = shark_compile_shader_extended((const char *)s->source, &candidate.size, s->type == GL_FRAGMENT_SHADER ? SHARK_FRAGMENT_SHADER : SHARK_VERTEX_SHADER, compiler_opts, compiler_fastmath, compiler_fastprecision, compiler_fastint);
 	if (output && candidate.size) {
 		SceGxmProgram *res = (SceGxmProgram *)vglMalloc(candidate.size);
